Okay, hearing none. Let's move on to item three, which is our auditor presentation.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:04.840
Michael, welcome. I appreciate you coming today.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.640
And the floor is yours.

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:14.795
>> Alright, well thank you very much. Again, my name is Mike Van Diebenter and I am a partner at Mahomes stable

00:01:14.955 --> 00:01:16.715
and ultimately responsible

00:01:16.715 --> 00:01:21.595
for overseeing the audit work for the town's fiscal year twenty twenty audit

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:28.820
in issuing the reports on behalf of the firm. So hopefully everybody has seen a copy of the financial

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:30.980
statements and single audit reports.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:35.940
My presentation will ultimately provide an overview of the work that was performed,

00:01:36.545 --> 00:01:40.625
the reports that were issued. I'll provide some overall

00:01:40.785 --> 00:01:42.705
high level financial highlights,

00:01:42.865 --> 00:01:46.865
and then certainly we'll answer any questions that any of you may have.

00:01:47.185 --> 00:01:51.585
At this point, I'm going to share my screen and actually share the presentation that I'll run through.

00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:09.675
Right, can everybody see the presentation at this point?

00:02:10.795 --> 00:02:11.515
Yep.

00:02:13.195 --> 00:02:14.395
All right, perfect.

00:02:17.755 --> 00:02:29.570
>> All right, so as far as the scope of work was performed, again, we did perform an audit of the town's financial statements. Performed that audit in accordance with both the auditing standards issued by the American Institute of Certified Public Accounts,

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:34.130
as well as the government auditing standards issued by the Government Accountability Office.

00:02:34.575 --> 00:02:45.455
In addition, based on the level of state funding that was received, we were also required to perform a state single audit. And that audit was performed in accordance with the State Single Audit Act.

00:02:45.775 --> 00:02:55.500
In addition to the audits, we also perform agreed upon procedures on the end of school year reports that are provided by the school district to the

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.180
Department of Education.

00:02:57.180 --> 00:03:01.580
Again, those procedures are required by the state of Connecticut Department of Education.

00:03:02.245 --> 00:03:15.445
In addition to those attest services, we do also perform a number of non audit services for the town. So again, we do assist in the preparation of the financial statements as well as the schedule of expenditures of state financial assistance in related notes.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:23.520
In addition, we also assist in converting your governmental fund financial statements to your government wide financial statements.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:36.395
In terms of the audit reports that were issued, again, the main report is your report on the financial statements. We did issue unmodified clean opinions on your financial statements.

00:03:36.955 --> 00:03:38.635
Again, an unmodified

00:03:38.635 --> 00:03:44.555
opinion provides reasonable assurance that the financial statements are free from a material misstatement,

00:03:44.955 --> 00:03:46.555
whether due to error or fraud,

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:52.830
and that they've been prepared in accordance with accounting principles generally accepted in The United States.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:59.070
So again, our opinion does cover multiple statements within your financial statements, it covers your governmental activities,

00:03:59.465 --> 00:04:05.305
each of your major governmental funds, which includes your general fund, as well as your capital reserve funds.

00:04:05.625 --> 00:04:10.185
And then we express an opinion on what's considered to be the aggregate remaining fund information.

00:04:10.345 --> 00:04:15.065
And that includes all of your non major special revenue capital projects,

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:22.740
a grant permanent private purpose trust and agency funds. So again, a lot of information is included in the financial statements.

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:25.620
But ultimately, we issued an opinion that

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:29.940
basically tells an external user that you can rely on that information

00:04:31.445 --> 00:04:34.405
when reviewing the financial statements.

00:04:36.165 --> 00:04:49.990
In connection with the state single audit, we do issue a report on compliance and on internal control at the state financial assistance level. So here we are actually expressing an opinion on the town's compliance with your major state programs.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.070
For fiscal year 2020,

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:56.950
the total state financial assistance that was expended by the town was approximately 2,500,000.

00:04:57.625 --> 00:05:04.585
The majority of that is considered exempt from our testing the portion which was not was about 398,000.

00:05:04.825 --> 00:05:07.945
Your major programs were the town aid road program,

00:05:08.745 --> 00:05:14.600
and your school readiness program. Again, we issued unmodified clean opinions on your compliance over those programs.

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:19.320
And we did not identify any findings that were required to again be reported.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:30.575
Again, for both the Town Aid Road program and school readiness program, the major compliance requirement is allowable costs. So again, we're testing costs that are charged these grants to determine that they're allowed.

00:05:33.375 --> 00:05:37.535
In addition, we also issue a report on compliance

00:05:37.535 --> 00:05:40.735
and on internal control over financial reporting.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:47.920
Unlike the previous two reports, I do like to point out that we do not actually express an opinion on the town's

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:50.640
effectiveness of your internal control,

00:05:50.880 --> 00:05:55.280
nor do we express an opinion on the town's compliance with

00:05:54.885 --> 00:06:06.805
regulations that actually doesn't fall within the scope of the audit. Essentially, during the course of performing the audit, if we became aware of or identified what we consider to be a material non compliance of a law regulation.

00:06:07.560 --> 00:06:11.480
And again, that non compliance would have a have to have a direct immaterial

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:13.480
impact on your financial statements,

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:15.800
meaning it could result in a loss,

00:06:16.680 --> 00:06:21.560
or a material weakness or significant deficiency in your internal control,

00:06:21.885 --> 00:06:24.845
were required to include it in this in this report.

00:06:25.165 --> 00:06:28.605
So again, we did end up reporting three significant

00:06:28.605 --> 00:06:30.765
deficiencies in internal controls.

00:06:31.165 --> 00:06:35.245
And again, a significant deficiency is a deficiency in internal control

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:43.350
that merits the attention of those charged with governance. So again, from a Board of Finance perspective, we felt that each of these items

00:06:43.590 --> 00:06:45.270
should be reported.

00:06:45.670 --> 00:06:47.670
Ultimately, the town is required to

00:06:48.745 --> 00:06:52.505
complete a corrective action plan and follow-up on these findings.

00:06:52.665 --> 00:06:55.945
So again, the first deficiency that was reported

00:06:56.025 --> 00:06:56.585
was

00:06:56.905 --> 00:07:00.425
a true significant deficiency in internal control over financial reporting.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:04.400
Again, do want to point out this is this is a repeat finding

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:13.280
from the prior year. And I do expect that this would be a finding that will ultimately get reported in connection with your fiscal year twenty twenty one audit,

00:07:13.845 --> 00:07:23.525
as this will ultimately get addressed in connection with your implementation of your new accounting system, which didn't occur until 07/01/2021.

00:07:24.005 --> 00:07:27.045
So again, the condition is that your accounting structure

00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:29.290
really is not properly

00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:31.450
set up within the general ledger system.

00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:38.810
As a result, manual reconciliations are required in order to provide the necessary information for financial reporting purposes.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:43.290
Ultimately, the recommendation is to overhaul your accounting system

00:07:43.905 --> 00:07:50.625
and no longer utilize balance sheet accounts to actually record revenues and expenditures relating to your governmental funds.

00:07:50.865 --> 00:07:55.665
So again, this is something that is being addressed in connection with your conversion to the new system.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:07:59.840
The next item here

00:08:00.400 --> 00:08:05.440
was a reporting of a significant deficiency in internal control over ACH disbursements.

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:08.560
I do know that the board was aware of the transaction

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.640
where an ACH fraud was perpetrated,

00:08:11.235 --> 00:08:14.595
whereby a vendor payment was made to a fraudulent bank account.

00:08:15.235 --> 00:08:19.635
Again, although this was not specifically identified as part of the audit procedures,

00:08:19.795 --> 00:08:21.555
it still does represent

00:08:21.555 --> 00:08:22.915
a reportable

00:08:22.915 --> 00:08:23.395
finding.

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:31.280
So again, we do recommend that the town implement procedures that require authentication and independent verification of vendor bank information.

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:36.240
Authentication should be obtained by requiring the vendor to provide a check,

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:38.560
deposit slip and or old banking information,

00:08:39.275 --> 00:08:43.995
and ultimately contacting the vendor to verify the information on hand. So

00:08:44.395 --> 00:08:47.675
unfortunately, with the increase in electronic banking,

00:08:47.915 --> 00:08:49.515
in general, we have seen

00:08:50.075 --> 00:08:51.915
this type of fraud occurring

00:08:52.635 --> 00:08:53.915
pretty commonly

00:08:54.670 --> 00:08:56.830
within businesses and governments.

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:58.990
And it's not just restricted to

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:00.590
vendor payments,

00:09:00.750 --> 00:09:02.750
direct deposits for employees.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:06.190
So again, it's really important to kind of tighten up those controls,

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:09.950
changing in any banking information should ultimately be verified

00:09:10.535 --> 00:09:14.695
in email should not be relied upon as that main correspondence.

00:09:17.095 --> 00:09:28.470
And then the last item here that we had was a deficiency in internal control over payroll. Again, this was identified by the town, it wasn't identified as part of the audit process, but still represents a reportable finding,

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:31.910
where an employee was paid an incorrect rate during the year.

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:36.870
So again, we recommend the pay rate documentation form be utilized to document

00:09:37.325 --> 00:09:38.845
every employee's pay.

00:09:39.165 --> 00:09:45.325
That form should ultimately be reviewed and approved by an appropriate town official and should be maintained in their employee records.

00:09:46.045 --> 00:09:53.485
And then again, an appropriate town official should periodically perform a document or review of all payroll records to verify that pay rates

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.270
agree with employee record.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:58.710
So again, I know both of these items were

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:05.110
the board was aware of, and ultimately they've been addressed, but they do still represent findings in connection with the audit.

00:10:07.285 --> 00:10:12.085
Any questions as far as the overall reporting before I move on to the financial highlights?

00:10:15.045 --> 00:10:17.605
Okay, so again, just giving you some overall

00:10:18.590 --> 00:10:22.990
financial highlights. Again, there's a lot of financial information included in the financial statements.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:26.350
Again, well over 100 pages of information.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:32.270
So certainly if you have any specific questions, I'm happy to answer those at any point in time.

00:10:32.975 --> 00:10:44.415
But in terms of your overall financial highlights, this first slide goes over your general fund on a budgetary basis. So again, your original budget did provide for the utilization of fund balance in the amount of 976,000

00:10:44.415 --> 00:10:46.655
to balance your revenues and expenditures.

00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:51.470
Your final budget did include additional appropriations of 240,000.

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:56.750
So that did result in a plan use of fund balance in the amount of about 1,200,000,

00:10:57.150 --> 00:11:03.945
your actual change in fund balance for the year was a decrease of 1,069,433.

00:11:03.945 --> 00:11:09.305
And so that resulted in overall favorable budgetary variance of 146,000.

00:11:09.465 --> 00:11:12.345
So again, if you if you plan to use 1.2,

00:11:12.345 --> 00:11:13.545
and you only use the million,

00:11:14.030 --> 00:11:18.110
