00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:19.230
Overall,

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:26.030
your actual revenues were approximately 95,000 more than budgeted, and that really was generated by a revenue surplus

00:11:26.815 --> 00:11:30.335
driven by favorable collections on your current year property taxes.

00:11:30.655 --> 00:11:37.135
And then again, your actual expenditures were approximately 45,000 less than budgeted, and there were budgetary surpluses

00:11:37.135 --> 00:11:39.295
across all departments at the end of the year.

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:53.480
This next slide goes over your governmental fund financial highlights. So this includes your general fund on a GAAP basis, as well as your capital reserve funds, all of your special revenue and other governmental

00:11:53.480 --> 00:11:53.880
funds.

00:11:54.345 --> 00:11:59.065
Your combined ending fund balances totaled approximately 4,400,000.

00:11:59.225 --> 00:12:02.505
So again, that was a decrease of about 335,000

00:12:02.505 --> 00:12:03.865
from the prior year.

00:12:04.585 --> 00:12:06.585
Of the 4,400,000

00:12:06.665 --> 00:12:09.225
to about 2,000,000 just over 2,000,000

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:13.630
was your fund balance in your general fund, again, was a decrease of

00:12:13.950 --> 00:12:16.510
1,069,433

00:12:16.510 --> 00:12:17.790
from the prior year.

00:12:18.430 --> 00:12:21.230
And again, that was driven by the plan use of your fund balance

00:12:21.835 --> 00:12:35.595
Of the 2,000,000 of your fund balance in the general fund four fifteen had been assigned for use in your fiscal year twenty twenty one budget. And so that left the remainder of $1,636,894

00:12:35.595 --> 00:12:40.690
as your unassigned fund balance, which would be available for appropriation.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:43.570
So that represents about 13.1%

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:48.130
of your fiscal year twenty twenty one General Fund budgetary expenditure appropriations,

00:12:48.290 --> 00:12:54.185
which again is sufficient to cover about one point five months of your overall General Fund budgetary expenditures.

00:12:54.505 --> 00:12:58.265
So again, I think in fiscal year eighteen, you had a very high

00:12:58.585 --> 00:13:00.265
percentage of fund balance,

00:13:00.665 --> 00:13:05.065
you have brought that down by offsetting your increases in taxes.

00:13:05.385 --> 00:13:09.465
And right now, as of June 30, you had about 13%

00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:11.210
available in your unassigned fund balance.

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:17.930
In terms of your capital reserve fund that had a ending fund balance of about 1,500,000,

00:13:17.930 --> 00:13:20.570
which was an increase of about 713,000

00:13:20.570 --> 00:13:21.610
from the prior year,

00:13:22.315 --> 00:13:31.915
That increase was really generated by a budgetary transfers from the general fund. So you've appropriated money from the general fund for specific projects.

00:13:32.155 --> 00:13:34.475
And so those are included in your capital reserve funds.

00:13:35.360 --> 00:13:38.240
Those amounts are committed for specific purposes.

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:43.280
And then all of your other funds had a fund balance of about 850,000,

00:13:43.280 --> 00:13:45.520
