00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:53.805
And again, those amounts are also restricted or committed for various purposes. So again, the positive thing is you had no negative fund balances

00:13:54.365 --> 00:13:57.165
that would ultimately impact your general fund budget.

00:14:01.245 --> 00:14:07.470
So before we move on to our required communications, again, just a brief highlight of your financials.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:15.070
Certainly if identified anything that I thought was of significance or concern from a financial perspective, would include it in these highlights.

00:14:19.625 --> 00:14:22.745
All right, so the last section is our required communications.

00:14:22.745 --> 00:14:26.425
And again, these communications are required by our auditing standards.

00:14:26.745 --> 00:14:46.010
The first item here talks about our responsibility under our auditing standards. Although we do assist in the preparation of the financial statements, they are the responsibility of management, all of the information included in the financial statements ultimately came from the town. Again, it's our responsibility to perform our audit procedures and express an opinion on those financial statements.

00:14:46.635 --> 00:14:52.715
In terms of the overall plan scope and timing of the audits, again, no changes in the overall scope of work that was performed.

00:14:52.875 --> 00:14:56.875
Again, multiple extensions were required from OPM.

00:14:57.195 --> 00:15:04.630
Delays in issuing the audit were attributed to really delay in the commencement of audit field work due to scheduling constraints.

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:10.230
Additional delays were resulted as a result of transition of key town personnel.

00:15:10.870 --> 00:15:18.525
And again, there were some additional delays resulting from having to perform the audit work remotely this past year due to the COVID-nineteen pandemic.

00:15:19.005 --> 00:15:24.605
The positive thing is we've already been out to start our planning for the fiscal year twenty one audit.

00:15:25.565 --> 00:15:29.480
And right now we have that scheduled so that it can be performed

00:15:29.800 --> 00:15:36.200
in your financial statements can ultimately be issued by the end of the year. Again, that is contingent upon ultimately

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:39.000
the closeout of the of the town's books and records.

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:43.685
But from a from a firm perspective, we have been able to move

00:15:43.925 --> 00:15:46.885
your timing into our normal business season.

00:15:48.805 --> 00:15:54.005
In terms of significant audit findings, we do look at your accounting policies and practices.

00:15:55.250 --> 00:16:00.290
One of the important things that we typically will point out is any implementation of any new accounting standards.

00:16:00.530 --> 00:16:03.570
So there were no new accounting standards that were ultimately

00:16:04.050 --> 00:16:11.895
implemented by the town. The GASB did issue a statement which postponed the effective date of certain authoritative guidance.

00:16:12.215 --> 00:16:18.615
And so that resulted in a postponement of the majority of GASB standards by at least one year in response to the pandemic.

00:16:19.175 --> 00:16:21.575
So again, no new standards were implemented

00:16:22.055 --> 00:16:24.455
in your fiscal year 2020 financials.

00:16:25.910 --> 00:16:26.790
Difficulties

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:33.350
that were encountered in performing the audit really just related to the timing issues and the delays that were previously discussed.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:42.735
Again, ultimately everything that we requested from the town was provided to us so that we could perform our audit work. There were no uncorrected misstatements.

00:16:42.975 --> 00:16:48.255
Any adjustments that were identified in connection where the audit were posed and recorded by the town.

00:16:48.575 --> 00:16:54.910
There were no disagreements with management during the course of performing the audits. We do obtain a management representation

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:55.550
letter.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.870
Again, there was nothing unusual

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.670
that we required management to represent to

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:01.710
in

00:17:02.110 --> 00:17:09.725
that letter. So again, for example, if we were unable to substantiate a transaction, and we relied on the representation of management,

00:17:09.885 --> 00:17:13.325
that would be a specific representation that we would communicate to you.

00:17:13.645 --> 00:17:18.205
Again, we weren't aware of any consultations by management with any other independent accounts.

00:17:19.200 --> 00:17:21.1000
So that includes all of our required communications.

00:17:22.080 --> 00:17:25.200
Again, happy to answer any questions that you may have.

